# ⚠️ index.html — A BUILT FILE (build.py glues src/shell.html + src/app/*.js).
# Without this line git merges it as ordinary text, and a merge of two branches
# can produce a CONSISTENT-LOOKING but inconsistent build — pieces of two
# different builds with no conflict and no warning. The mine was found by
# INTERFACE 2026-07-29 (that time the auto-merge happened to coincide with an
# honest rebuild byte-for-byte, i.e. we got lucky).
# `-merge` forces git to declare a CONFLICT instead of a silent glue-up: the
# resolution is always the same — `python3 build.py`, i.e. rebuild from sources.
# ⚠️ DO NOT REMOVE this line «so that it merges without conflicts»: the conflict
# here IS the protection.
index.html -merge
# ⚠️ bonus.html — THE SAME KIND OF BUILT SINGLE-FILE BUNDLE (a snapshot of the
# claude/bonus-standalone branch with the bonus level removed, 2026-08-18). Its
# mine is the same one, and it stays just as silent: without `-merge` git glues
# two different snapshots with no conflict. The resolution differs from
# index.html — not a rebuild, but
# `git show claude/bonus-standalone:index.html > bonus.html`.
bonus.html -merge
